{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Moses spoke to the heads of the tribes etc. This is the thing that HaShem commanded.</b> The Rashbam asked: where do we find that Moses was commanded concerning the passage of vows? And he answered that it is written above: ״אלה תעשו לה' במועדיכם לבד מנדריכם״ — that is, vows and freewill offerings that a person vows and donates of his own will; but there are other vows that have a different law, and that verse refers back to what is written at the beginning of the offerings: ״וידבר ה' אל משה לאמר״."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:21.686366155Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}